<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="viewer-match-day" data-rev="2">
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> web/match-state.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">Pure reducer from events to the match state at a tick. Events are released by the rendered tick, never by arrival, because the stream leads playback by up to 500 ticks.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web/ state</td><td>+180</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/feed.mjs, scoreboard.mjs, goal-moment.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">Per-frame feed batcher with one fragment insert per frame; the 56-pixel header with crests, score bug, clock, and speed; the goal pulse, banner, and highlight inside 1.5 seconds, with reduced motion respected.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web/ panels</td><td>+400</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/lineups.mjs, stats.mjs (source pending Q-1)</summary><div class="pl-card">Lineup rows with fatigue bar and a state word beside every colour; the nine-row statistics grid. The roster, fatigue, and statistics fields do not exist on the wire today.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web/ panels</td><td>+290</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/components/panels.css</summary><div class="pl-card">Score bug, banner, feed, lineup, and statistics styles on the existing tokens; opacity and transform transitions only.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web/ page</td><td>+220</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/index.html, main.mjs, layout.css, tokens.css, pitch.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">Panel markup replaces the empty regions; one flush per frame from the rendered tick; a read-only matchDay() hook; full time named apart from a dropped stream; parked markers hidden.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>web/ page</td><td>+178 / -41</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> web/tests/match-state, feed, stats, lineups; helpers (modified)</summary><div class="pl-card">Goal visible at its tick and not before; a 40-event burst inserted with none dropped; every statistics field equal; every fatigue band carries a word.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web/tests</td><td>+400</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> crates/protocol, crates/engine-cli, crates/engine, docs/reference/protocol.md (pending Q-1)</summary><div class="pl-card">Roster, running statistics, and player energy on the wire. The engine already keeps every value; only the message shape is open. Not decided by this plan: the product owner chooses the wire shape (additive fields at the same version, new messages at a new version, or roster from the team files with only statistics and energy on the wire).</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/ and docs</td><td>+185 / -5</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R1 · Q-1 open: no roster, fatigue, or live statistics on the wire</div><div class="callout-body">The engine now keeps all nine statistics and each player's energy, but no message carries them or the roster. The wire shape is a contract decision; the plan is awaiting input with three options recorded.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R2 · Events arrive ahead of playback</div><div class="callout-body">Showing an event on arrival would announce a goal before the pitch draws it. Events are released by the rendered tick, tested with a goal arriving 400 ticks early.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R3 · Panels steal frame budget</div><div class="callout-body">One flush per frame, changed nodes only, statistics per message and never per tick.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R4 · No reduced-motion emulation in the browser tool</div><div class="callout-body">A proxy attribute shares the media query's CSS block; the real query is checked when the operator turns off Windows animation effects.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R8 · A later event-contract redesign renames event kinds</div><div class="callout-body">A planned later programme moves event kinds to provider names, raises the protocol version, and may carry about 1,400 events a match. The new modules keep every event-kind string in one table, and the feed batcher does not depend on the event count.</div></aside>
  </div>
  <details class="pl-revs"><summary>2 prior revisions</summary><ul><li>rev 0 (2026-09-22): first plan, awaiting input on Q-1 (scope here, re-sequence, or proposed contract). Superseded because the producer slices have since shipped.</li><li>rev 1 (2026-09-23): auto-review re-grounded on the shipped producers; Q-1 narrowed to the wire shape with three options. Superseded by a drift review that adds the event-contract redesign risk.</li></ul></details>
  <style>
    .fragment-plan .pl-files { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-files th, .fragment-plan .pl-files td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.25); vertical-align: top; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-files summary { cursor: pointer; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-chip { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.7rem; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid currentColor; margin-right: 6px; opacity: 0.8; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-card { padding: 6px 0 4px 18px; opacity: 0.9; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-risks { display: grid; gap: 8px; margin-top: 12px; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-revs { margin-top: 12px; }
    @media (max-width: 480px) { .fragment-plan .pl-files th:nth-child(3), .fragment-plan .pl-files td:nth-child(3) { display: none; } }
  </style>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-plan');
      var files = 26, modules = 6;
      var risks = root ? root.querySelectorAll('.pl-risks .callout').length : 0;
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', { detail: { name: 'plan', artifact: 'plan', counts: { files: files, modules: modules, risks: risks } } }));
    })();
  </script>
</section>
